From: Arch POWER
Subject: [PATCH] audio/pipewire: cast proxy for pw_node_enum_params()

pipewire 0.3.8x exposed pw_node_enum_params() as a macro that accepted
any proxy. Newer pipewire (1.6) declares it as a real function taking
struct pw_node *, so passing the pw_proxy * is now a hard error under
GCC 14+, where -Wincompatible-pointer-types is an error by default:

  SDL_pipewire.c:593:37: error: passing argument 1 of pw_node_enum_params
                                from incompatible pointer type
  node.h:208: expected struct pw_node * but argument is of type struct pw_proxy *

The proxy is the node object; the cast is what the old macro did
implicitly.

---
--- a/src/audio/pipewire/SDL_pipewire.c
+++ b/src/audio/pipewire/SDL_pipewire.c
@@ -590,7 +590,7 @@
 
         /* Need to parse the parameters to get the sample rate */
         for (i = 0; i < info->n_params; ++i) {
-            pw_node_enum_params(node->proxy, 0, info->params[i].id, 0, 0, NULL);
+            pw_node_enum_params((struct pw_node *)node->proxy, 0, info->params[i].id, 0, 0, NULL);
         }
 
         hotplug_core_sync(node);
